        "Start with the weather. Raichur district sits in a semi-arid belt, with average annual rainfall listed at roughly 680 mm, and April and May afternoons commonly pass 40 degrees. Karnataka's schools close for summer in that stretch, and it is also when IB Diploma papers and the Cambridge May-June series fall. A Lingsugur student sitting papers in another city should arrive early and rehearse a hot, silent exam hall.",
        "Festivals shape the year more than most families expect. Dasara brings a long holiday in late September or October, Deepavali follows, then Sankranti in January and Ugadi in March or April. Muharram and Maha Shivaratri are both described as important in Lingsugur itself, and both follow lunar calendars, so their dates move each year. We ask for the school calendar and the family's own list of dates at the start of every term and plan around both.",
        "Farming sets a rhythm too. Raichur is known as the rice bowl of Karnataka and holds a cotton trading market, and families who farm or trade often have a heavy fortnight at harvest or sowing. A student who loses a week then needs a shorter, sharper session pattern, not a missed month. We build one catch-up slot into the plan instead of pretending the week did not happen.",
        "On the examination side, the Karnataka SSLC and pre-university papers fall in March, while an international candidate may be preparing for a Cambridge or Edexcel series in January, March, May-June or October-November, or for the IB's May session. Where a child works towards one of these alongside State Board papers, the sensible approach is to rank the exams by date and weight and split the term accordingly.",
