        "Tier comes first because it caps the grade. A Core entry at Cambridge tops out at a mid-range grade, while Extended opens the full scale; Pearson Edexcel's Foundation and Higher tiers work the same way. A family with nobody locally to ask often guesses, and a wrong guess shows up two years later as a Diploma Mathematics course that feels like a wall.",
        "A diagnostic session settles most cases. The tutor sets a few Extended-level questions, watches how the student reasons, and notes where the algebra or the units wobble. If the student cannot yet handle those but is improving fast, Extended with extra support is often better than a safe Core entry that closes doors. If the student is stretched in every subject, Core in some subjects may be the kinder choice.",
