  faqs: [
    { question: "Where can I find an IB tutor in Lingsugur?", answer: "You will not find a specialist in the taluk, so the practical answer is an online tutor chosen for your child's exact subject and level. IB Gram shortlists from tutors across India who have taught that course recently, and every class runs live on video on IST. Send the programme, subject, level and exam sitting, and a free trial lesson is arranged first so you can judge the teaching before deciding anything." },
    { question: "Can my child get IGCSE home tuition in Lingsugur?", answer: "Yes, as online home tuition: a private lesson the student attends from home on a laptop or tablet, with the tutor teaching live. Both Cambridge and Pearson Edexcel IGCSE are covered, at Core or Extended and Foundation or Higher tiers. The tutor is chosen for the specification the school has actually entered the student for, and the lesson uses past papers from that board." },
    { question: "Will a tutor come to our house in Lingsugur?", answer: "No. IB Gram's tutors do not visit homes in Lingsugur; in-person home visits exist only in Gurugram and parts of Delhi NCR. Here the lesson happens on screen, with the tutor writing on a shared whiteboard while the student works at home. All a family needs is a laptop or tablet, headphones, a steady connection and a quiet corner." },
    { question: "Which schools in or near Lingsugur teach the IB or IGCSE?", answer: "None that we can confirm. The Raichur school listing we checked shows a CBSE school and no IB or Cambridge school, and our checks in Lingsugur taluk found none either. The nearest confirmed options are the International School of Hyderabad (IB Diploma) and The Gaudium School (Cambridge IGCSE and AS & A Level), about 300 km away, and Stonehill International School in Bengaluru (full IB continuum), which also takes boarders." },
    { question: "How much does IB or IGCSE tuition cost for a student in Lingsugur?", answer: "There is no published price list. The rate depends on the programme and level, the subject, the length of each session and how scarce the specialism is, so Higher Level Diploma sciences sit above IGCSE Core subjects. Lingsugur families pay the same as anyone else because no travel is involved. You receive the rate in writing before booking, and the first lesson costs nothing." },
    { question: "Is the internet in Lingsugur good enough for live online lessons?", answer: "Usually yes if the connection is stable, though we cannot promise any particular provider's line. A lesson needs a steady link rather than a fast one: video and a shared whiteboard run comfortably on ordinary broadband or good 4G. Use the free trial as the test, keep a phone hotspot ready as a backup, and put the laptop on charge before class in case the power dips." },
    { question: "Can a child from a Kannada-medium or State Board school move to IGCSE or the IB?", answer: "Yes, and many students do, though the first term needs care. The content gap is usually smaller than the gap in exam language: command words, extended answers and English subject vocabulary. We start with a diagnostic lesson, then build vocabulary and written-answer habits alongside the syllabus. Moving at Class 8 or 9 is easier than at Class 11, but a later switch is workable with focused teaching." },
    { question: "Can my child sit Cambridge IGCSE exams from Lingsugur without joining a Cambridge school?", answer: "Cambridge accepts private candidates through registered exam centres, but centres are thin outside the metros and each sets its own conditions, so contact the centre first. IB Gram does not run exams or act as a centre. We prepare the student for the papers, and the family arranges entry through a centre. Practical papers may need laboratory access, so ask the centre what it provides." },
    { question: "Which IB subjects can your tutors cover?", answer: "Mathematics Analysis and Approaches and Applications and Interpretation, the three sciences, Economics, Business Management, English A, Computer Science, Psychology, Geography, History, Environmental Systems and Societies and Hindi B, along with Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay coaching. MYP and PYP are covered as well. A less common subject can usually be matched, from a shorter list of specialists." },
    { question: "Do tutors help with the IB Internal Assessment and Extended Essay?", answer: "They coach; they do not write. A tutor can help narrow a research question, explain what each criterion rewards, check a method, and give feedback on a draft the student wrote alone. Producing text that carries the student's name, whether an IA, an Extended Essay, a TOK essay or coursework, is outside what any IB Gram tutor does, because the IB treats that as misconduct." },
    { question: "Will the IB or IGCSE be accepted for NEET, JEE or Karnataka colleges?", answer: "Generally yes through equivalence, but the details belong to each admitting body. The Association of Indian Universities issues equivalence for the IB Diploma and IGCSE, NEET UG and JEE ask for particular subjects at Class 12 level, and CUET-UG serves central universities. For state seats, ask the Karnataka Examinations Authority how study outside the region is treated. We do not guarantee admission anywhere; we teach the subjects." },
    { question: "When should a Lingsugur student start IB or IGCSE tuition?", answer: "Start when the course starts if you can: Grade 9 for IGCSE, Class 11 for the Diploma, and Class 8 if a move to an English-medium school is planned. That leaves time to fix gaps before internal exams, Internal Assessments and predicted grades converge. Starting in the exam year still helps if sessions go to high-yield topics, with a plan for the hot April weeks." },
    { question: "What time slots work for students in Lingsugur?", answer: "Weekday evenings after school and weekend mornings cover most bookings. In April and May the slot moves earlier or later to avoid the hottest hours, and around Dasara, Deepavali and harvest weeks we shift it to suit the household. Ahead of mocks or an exam series, a second weekly class is easy to add. All tutors teach on IST, so there is no time-zone adjustment." },
    { question: "What if the tutor is not the right fit for my child?", answer: "Tell us and a different tutor is arranged; changing is part of the arrangement, not a favour. Reviews every few weeks are meant to catch a poor fit early, and the written note after each class gives you something concrete to point to. You never need to argue for a change." },
    { question: "Do you teach younger children in PYP or MYP, or only Diploma students?", answer: "The whole range is covered. Younger PYP children get shorter, more frequent sessions built around reading, number and the questions they ask about their Exhibition. MYP students work on criterion-based writing in the sciences and Individuals and Societies, and on shaping a Personal Project early. Diploma and IGCSE tutoring completes the range." },
    { question: "Is IB Gram connected to any school, the IB or Cambridge?", answer: "No. IB Gram is an independent tutoring service with no affiliation to any school named on this page, to the International Baccalaureate, to Cambridge or to Pearson. Schools are named only to show where the nearest IB and Cambridge options are, and none appears here as a partner or sponsor." },
  ],

